["The base is a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space, including zero dimension. Both global Hessian bounds, ContDiff order2, positive eta and beta eta≤1 are the displayed input assumptions.","Measure.tilted is normalized exponential tilting. The displayed joint law is an independent-product Gaussian pushforward; its marginals, reflected pushforward, every-state normalized kernel and stationary disintegration are conclusions.","Lp exponent2 is the complete real space of measurable square-integrable almost-everywhere classes. lpMeas consists of classes measurable with respect to the displayed comap sigma algebra. The displayed Fact(comap≤product) is derived internally from measurable_snd and supplies closedness; it is not a public binder.","condExpL2 is L² conditional expectation. HP.subtypeL is inclusion, HP.orthogonalProjectionOnto takes an ambient class into the closed subspace, and range equality and the canonical pullback isometric equivalence are conclusions.","Operator multiplication is composition; adjoint composition B.adjoint∘L B acts on the domain of B. IsPositive means selfadjointness and nonnegative quadratic form. conjStarAlgEquiv by an isometry e sends C to e C e.symm. Full-joint identity and identity on HP have different domains.","Scalar root and the SAME transported macro root are internally produced. Their energy equalities quantify over every macro class; the later EVERY positive same-square macro alternative equals the root with no alternative energy premise. Literal reflection and conditional action are per-observable AE, while normalized kernel density holds every state."]